Model lists read top to bottom, and the last button is reachable
=================================================================

Two things a person hits in their first two minutes.

**Every model list is alphabetical.** The order a vendor published in is not an order — it is the
accident of their release schedule — and a list you scan has to be predictable. The prefilled default
for Ollama Cloud is still DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, because a default that moves is worse than one that is
merely not your favourite; the list around it is simply sorted.

**Onboarding survives a small window.** At a quarter-screen the Connect button sat below the fold with
nothing to scroll, so the only way to finish was to maximise the window first. The first-run page now
scrolls, and compacts its own spacing below 700px tall and 900px wide rather than shrinking the type.

**And Enter submits.** In the key field, in the provider select, in the old-hand table — because the
key is the last thing anybody types, and hunting for a button afterwards is a step that exists for no
reason.

